WEBVTT

1
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,554
[rooster crowing]

2
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:22,230
[wind blowing, leaves rustling]

3
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:30,613
[phone ringing]

4
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:36,995
Hello?

5
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,830
[woman] <i>Hello? Modesta?</i>

6
00:00:40,373 --> 00:00:41,291
Who's calling?

7
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:44,544
[man] All right, I'll make it work, madam.

8
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,464
Dencio, we're back in business.

9
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:49,382
Cake, you seen Jo?

10
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:51,009
{\an8}Here, Director.

11
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:53,094
{\an8}The network wants Dencio back.

12
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:56,264
{\an8}Yes, but I'm sure we shot Dencio.
He's dead.

13
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:58,808
{\an8}Who wants to see this show canceled?

14
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:00,727
{\an8}-No one.
-[all] No!

15
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:03,396
{\an8}Okay, then how do we bring him back
from the dead?

16
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,024
{\an8}Perhaps it's a nightmare, or he's a ghost,
reincarnation?

17
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:08,109
{\an8}It's an action series, all right,
not a fantasy.

18
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,277
{\an8}Jo, you're the writer.

19
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,905
{\an8}-Think about it.
-Right, at this point, I don't know.

20
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:14,657
{\an8}-Spirits, maybe?
-Spirits is a little far out.

21
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,701
{\an8}-[woman] Take the glass.
-Excuse me, director.

22
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,203
{\an8}What if there's a twin?

23
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:20,038
{\an8}[gulps]

24
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,499
{\an8}Twins. Case closed!

25
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:23,625
{\an8}Make up for Dencio.

26
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,251
{\an8}[all cheering]

27
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:27,378
{\an8}God damn it, Matti!

28
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:29,881
{\an8}If you didn't pack that bag,
I'm gonna fucking kill you!

29
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:32,926
{\an8}Mom, wtf I told you I brought it.
You reminded me, like, 500 times.

30
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:35,178
{\an8}-Really?
-Yes. Five hundred times.

31
00:01:35,261 --> 00:01:36,429
{\an8}-500?
-Yes. I counted.

32
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:37,931
{\an8}-Spare me the math.
-Shut up.

33
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,642
{\an8}And will you stop sounding so smart.

34
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:42,060
{\an8}You're such a little shit!

35
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:46,147
{\an8}Hey, are you here to drive us?

36
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,732
{\an8}Ma'am Paz De Los Santos?

37
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:49,150
{\an8}Don't call me ma'am.

38
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:51,152
{\an8}-I'm not that old.
-Let me take that, ma'am.

39
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,487
{\an8}-Get in the car.
-I've got this.

40
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:54,864
{\an8}-Be careful.
-Hey, move along.

41
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:55,865
{\an8}Time's up.

42
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,493
{\an8}Don't call me ma'am. [sarcastically]

43
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,869
{\an8}Shit. Is this true?

44
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:02,413
{\an8}Yes. Your dad's picking her up
from the pier.

45
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:04,499
{\an8}I need to get to set now.

46
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:05,834
{\an8}I'll call you later, mom.

47
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:07,752
{\an8}Hello, dear?

48
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:09,963
{\an8}[sighs]

49
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:11,422
{\an8}The buried have arisen.

50
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:12,882
{\an8}Who?

51
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,425
{\an8}The one who went AWOL.

52
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:17,720
{\an8}-They've returned.
-Your natural mother?

53
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,640
{\an8}Our lady of eternal absence?

54
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:23,059
{\an8}OMG.

55
00:02:23,768 --> 00:02:26,688
{\an8}The former starlet is making a comeback?

56
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:30,567
{\an8}[weather forecast on radio]

57
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:35,572
{\an8}This is fucking surreal.

58
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:40,160
{\an8}Welcome home!

59
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:41,911
{\an8}You're fucking weird, Mom.

60
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,329
{\an8}[both chuckle]

61
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:45,248
{\an8}Well, that workshop's another thing.

62
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:49,252
{\an8}They have so many requirements, they've
even asked for a sequence treatment.

63
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:51,796
{\an8}At least now my visa's ready.

64
00:02:52,922 --> 00:02:54,632
{\an8}I think you've got this, girl!

65
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:57,176
{\an8}You revived a dead body, didn't you?
Your bad!

66
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,846
{\an8}Eighteen sequences, on the spot.

67
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:01,264
{\an8}-I know you can--
-Girl.

68
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:03,558
{\an8}We're talking about <i>America.</i>

69
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:06,436
{\an8}Well, you never know,
they might hire you when you're there,

70
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:08,062
{\an8}Miss Shonda Rhimes!

71
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:11,190
{\an8}She might hire you, girl, think on that.

72
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:13,276
But wait…

73
00:03:13,359 --> 00:03:15,361
Can you really leave all this behind?

74
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:17,822
All this?

75
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:18,823
Yeah.

76
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:22,327
-Yeah.
-Yeah!

77
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,703
I'm ready to.

78
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:25,622
[ship horn blowing]

79
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:30,627
Wake up, Matias. Wake up.

80
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:31,628
What?

81
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:34,297
Just smell that.

82
00:03:35,506 --> 00:03:37,508
Smell it. It's… [inhales deeply]

83
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:40,261
-…pure ocean air.
-[coughs]

84
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:41,721
Are you okay?

85
00:03:41,804 --> 00:03:43,765
Yeah. Yeah. The ocean, yeah.

86
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:45,141
-Here.
-Thanks.

87
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:48,728
It's just so weird to be back, you know?

88
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:51,356
I'm sure they're all excited to see us.

89
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:53,399
Really?

90
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:55,568
I was famous, you know?

91
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:56,527
Mm-hmm.

92
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,528
I was!

93
00:04:00,156 --> 00:04:05,411
Once upon a time, I was
Manila's up and coming dramatic star.

94
00:04:06,204 --> 00:04:07,580
[chuckles]

95
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:09,499
Did you ever arrive?

96
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:11,417
[chuckles]

97
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:13,920
Watch it, or I'll send you overboard.

98
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:16,506
I think we're here.

99
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:21,886
[ship horn blowing]

100
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:26,599
{\an8}THIS, THAT AND EVERYTHING IN BETWEEN

101
00:04:38,486 --> 00:04:42,198
-Matti, watch the bag!
-Mom, they're not gonna run away.

102
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:47,620
[people chattering]

103
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:51,207
Rene!

104
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:55,503
Rene?

105
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,213
Is that you? Paz?

106
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:59,007
I don't believe it.

107
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:01,342
-Can you put those in the back?
-Who? Who's that?

108
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:02,427
Still your car?

109
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:06,723
You should know I'm not the kind of guy
who just throws broken things away.

110
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:07,724
Who's this?

111
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,101
My son.

112
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:12,145
-Welcome. Welcome. Welcome.
-Hi

113
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:14,022
-Make yourself at home.
-Thanks.

114
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,023
-Hurry up.
-Hop in.

115
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:17,275
[Paz] Thank you.

116
00:05:17,358 --> 00:05:18,318
Be careful, Matti.

117
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:19,861
[groans]

118
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:23,239
-[Paz] Does everything fit?
-Uh-huh.

119
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:24,782
Let's go.

120
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:25,950
Are you okay, Matti?

121
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,035
Yeah. Yeah.

122
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:28,286
Is the box up there?

123
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:29,287
Yeah.

124
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:50,975
There.

125
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:53,227
This old house waited for you.

126
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:02,945
I had Claro clean the house.

127
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:05,281
You remember our old helper?

128
00:06:05,364 --> 00:06:06,324
They were useless.

129
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,967
Jo uses your old room when she's here,

130
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:27,845
but she hardly ever comes home.

131
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,723
I've prepared your father's room.

132
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:32,600
Oh…

133
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:34,811
who have you brought with you?

134
00:06:40,149 --> 00:06:41,651
This is my youngest, Matti.

135
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:43,736
[Bes] Wow,

136
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,113
so handsome.

137
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:47,824
He looks like a celebrity.

138
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:48,908
Say hello to Manang.

139
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:51,035
He's just like his mother.

140
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:54,914
My God. Just give her a kiss.

141
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,754
Come on, come through here.

142
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:08,761
[Matti playing guitar]

143
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:14,433
[Paz] Matias!

144
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,227
Cut it out!

145
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,604
[guitar stops]

146
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:26,362
[cell phone ringing]

147
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:35,621
Dad.

148
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:38,499
[Rene] <i>Jo, darling, come home, please.</i>

149
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:39,667
<i>Your mom wants to see you.</i>

150
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:42,837
It's…

151
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:46,507
Dad, I have a lot of work here.

152
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:49,093
<i>Sweetheart, family comes first.</i>

153
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:51,554
<i>You can't just work all the time.</i>

154
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:55,099
<i>You haven't been here for a while.</i>

155
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:58,060
<i>Please come home.</i>

156
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:00,146
<i>You know, it's been a while</i>
<i>since I've seen you--</i>

157
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:03,774
-[groans softly]
<i>-What happened? Everything all right, Jo?</i>

158
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:05,610
Let me get back to you.

159
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,487
-At least think--
-Shit!

160
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:20,166
[Jo] It's just one thing after another.

161
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:22,251
Okay…

162
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:25,505
so tell me, let's look at that.

163
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:27,965
Just remember, you're in a safe space.

164
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:30,927
This workshop,
it's great. I'm not complaining.

165
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:35,014
I mean, this is my chance to…

166
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:39,101
to actually make a better life for myself.

167
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:44,482
It's just that I wonder now that
it's getting closer to being a reality,

168
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:48,653
if this is the right thing for me to do,
'cause…

169
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:50,238
'cause I feel, I don't know,

170
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:53,032
I feel like there's something missing.

171
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:57,662
I know this is a great move
and it could change my life, but…

172
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:00,623
I feel like…

173
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:04,669
I feel like there's
something I need to do first.

174
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:07,255
Are we talking mostly about
the trip right now, or…

175
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,924
is there something else bothering you?

176
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,310
I heard Paz is here.

177
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,440
[voice shaking]

178
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,112
My God!

179
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,575
She's back.

180
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:40,663
Just when I'm finally moving on
with my life,

181
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:43,583
I have to rip open wounds.

182
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:47,962
And my father wants me to be there at home

183
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:52,008
as if it's all okay now,
it's all fine.

184
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:55,553
I mean, now, I don't know this person.

185
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,848
She never cared for me.

186
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:02,101
That's what they don't understand.

187
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:06,105
That it took a lot for me
to get to this point.

188
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:10,359
Sure, family, it's important,

189
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:14,196
but tell me how you would react
if this was your family.

190
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:16,907
[sighs]

191
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:20,536
Then don't go.

192
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:23,164
Don't go.

193
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:26,459
You have your own life right now.

194
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,795
I have my own life.

195
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:30,796
It's your choice.

196
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:34,342
Remember what we talked about?

197
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,552
Personal boundaries.

198
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,472
Boundaries. Yes.

199
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:42,350
It's not a selfish thing to do, Jo.

200
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:43,893
Okay.

201
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,728
Boundaries.

202
00:10:48,147 --> 00:10:49,023
Yes.

203
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:50,024
Here…

204
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:52,193
your other hand.

205
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:55,988
Let's breathe.

206
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,073
Okay,

207
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,074
deep inhale.

208
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:02,036
-[inhales deeply]
-Two, three, four.

209
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:04,538
Hold and exhale.

210
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:08,250
-[exhales deeply]
-Two, three, four.

211
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,418
Hold.

212
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:10,836
{\an8}It's your choice.

213
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,838
{\an8}It's my choice.

214
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:15,174
{\an8}-It's my choice.
-Another one. Inhale.

215
00:11:15,257 --> 00:11:18,094
-[inhales deeply]
-Two, three, four.

216
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,261
Hold…

217
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,939
[ship horn blowing]

218
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,457
[ship horn blowing]

219
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:17,820
[yelps] Damn it!

220
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:20,322
-[chuckles]
-Pain in the ass.

221
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,323
[Rene] It's gone now.

222
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,076
What are you laughing about?

223
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,077
Such a waste.

224
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:35,671
Don't you get bored, Renato?

225
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:39,508
Not at all.

226
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:43,304
I don't think there's anything boring
about living peacefully.

227
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:48,642
-Can I ask you a question?
-Hmm.

228
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,728
What does that place have, that we don't?

229
00:12:51,729 --> 00:12:52,646
Where is <i>that</i>?

230
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:54,732
America.

231
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,443
We've got TV here,

232
00:12:57,526 --> 00:12:59,403
the movies and shows are no different.

233
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:05,409
What the fuck is your point, Renato?

234
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:08,662
Why did you have to go so far away?

235
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:17,129
Most things can be fixed, right?

236
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:20,799
Whether it's a big thing or a small thing,

237
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:23,886
you try and fix it
instead of just up and leaving.

238
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:31,060
That hurt me, you know, and Jo too.

239
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:36,106
You don't get me, I see that.

240
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:40,569
Well, you should have explained yourself
to me before you ran away.

241
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:47,952
I couldn't do that, for you.

242
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:54,291
Do you think you can explain yourself now?

243
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,006
[Paz] Shit.

244
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:05,928
{\an8}It's stuck.

245
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:11,684
Shit, shit, shit, shit, shit!

246
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,729
Fuck!

247
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:17,314
Fuck!

248
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:37,918
[exhales]

249
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,641
[Jo] Shit, shit, shit, shit!

250
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:54,685
[groans softly]

251
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,942
[dog marking]

252
00:15:05,946 --> 00:15:09,325
[both screaming]

253
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,412
Is that… Joanne?

254
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,122
Joanne!

255
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:17,750
Joanne!

256
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:18,918
Joanne!

257
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,210
-[Jo screams]
-[coughing]

258
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:26,133
Joanne?

259
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:30,304
Joanne, it's me!

260
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:34,391
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

261
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:38,562
-Joanne?
-I'm peeing!

262
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:41,106
Joanne, have you met your brother?

263
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,317
-Joanne?
-Brother?

264
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:46,320
Joanne, come out!

265
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:49,365
Joanne!

266
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:58,457
I'm so happy.

267
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,960
My two, full grown children together.

268
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:05,381
-Matti, meet your sister Joanne.
-It's Jo.

269
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:07,257
-Joanne, meet Matti.
-Jo.

270
00:16:09,468 --> 00:16:11,345
Gosh, look at you.

271
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:13,013
You're all grown up.

272
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:15,641
-The last time I saw you…
-I was ten.

273
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:17,768
Well, look at her, will you?

274
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:20,938
You look so much like each other.

275
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:26,652
We look so similar, don't you think?

276
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:27,778
Except for the nose.

277
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:32,157
And looks like you haven't slept
in years…

278
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:34,159
and you could do more carbs,

279
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,704
you know, just, you know,
for the meat of it.

280
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:39,373
Hey, how about you can
sleep in my bedroom?

281
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,002
-We could chit chat.
-Your bedroom?

282
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:44,336
Yes, my bedroom.

283
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,797
It's huge, the bed's enormous.

284
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,008
Or maybe you want wine.
You want wine?

285
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,760
-Or maybe a joint? All right, let's do it.
-I'm tired.

286
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:52,886
I'm tired.

287
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:55,472
Let's talk about my life in New York!

288
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,307
Joanne!

289
00:17:00,227 --> 00:17:02,521
Hey, who the hell is that?

290
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:05,816
You'll give a heart attack.

291
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:06,775
What time is it?

292
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:08,902
Can I stay here?

293
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:10,863
She's taken my room.

294
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:15,492
I'm glad you came home.

295
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,244
Wait there.

296
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:18,245
I need to pee.

297
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:23,459
How long will they stay?

298
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:24,668
I don't know.

299
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:25,669
Nobody knows.

300
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,422
[sighs softly]

301
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:33,177
Why?

302
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,098
Why?

303
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:44,772
She's your mother.

304
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,076
[Rene] You're a scoundrel.

305
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:58,952
I bet you're just after my money,
aren't you?

306
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:00,954
You think they still recognize me?

307
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:02,581
Why are they all staring?

308
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:05,375
Because you look like a bug lady.

309
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:06,585
Stop it! What's this?

310
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,421
Salted egg. Can you believe it?

311
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:11,381
-Yeah.
-Yeah. That's nice.

312
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:12,841
I missed these.

313
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,259
They're so good.

314
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:16,220
This is amazing.

315
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:19,014
Hey, you know, this is so Philippines.

316
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,225
-Are you hot now?
-Look, look, look.

317
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:23,227
Can I try this on?

318
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:24,228
Of course, ma'am.

319
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:28,315
-Do you think this works for me?
-Yeah, it looks nice. It looks very nice.

320
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:29,316
I'm not sure.

321
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:30,734
Just buy it. Come on.

322
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:32,486
It's Aunt Abby.

323
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:35,197
-Quick. Thanks.
-Rude.

324
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:37,866
-[Rene] Be careful.
-Paz!

325
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:39,910
Careful with the eggs,
I don't wanna break them.

326
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:41,995
-Is that you, Paz?
-Okay. Let's go.

327
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:43,372
Drive!

328
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:54,341
[Bes] Jo!

329
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:57,427
Tilapia. It was just caught.

330
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,388
-Mom, look at that.
-Yeah.

331
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:01,890
Rene, we can make ceviche with this.

332
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,102
[Rene] Sweetheart.

333
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:06,895
How long have you been here?

334
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:08,063
Since morning, Dad.

335
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,232
Good girl.

336
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:13,861
Have you had the pleasure
of meeting your brother?

337
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:18,157
I wonder if he was a premature baby…

338
00:19:19,616 --> 00:19:21,076
because he acts like…

339
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,288
he's not fully grown.

340
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:27,708
I gotta go get something.

341
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:36,508
Well, Paz, I said we'd bump
into that old lady eventually, right?

342
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,720
She's like a dog with a bone.

343
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:42,181
She doesn't miss a thing.

344
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,308
Wait…

345
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,227
did you only buy fruit and vegetables?

346
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:49,938
No.

347
00:19:51,773 --> 00:19:52,733
Here we go.

348
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:55,360
Rice. Look. Good job. There.

349
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,738
Now, that'll be perfect.

350
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:02,868
Now, I'll get that fish cooked
and serve it with the leftover rice.

351
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:04,620
And then I'll do that…

352
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:05,621
Do what?

353
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,041
Start making sense, will you?

354
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:10,167
Can you be more clear?

355
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,919
-I am being clear.
-[Bes screams outside]

356
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:12,961
It's Matti!

357
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:15,589
Huh?

358
00:20:15,672 --> 00:20:16,924
[Bes] Hey!

359
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:18,467
Hey, Matti!

360
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:20,219
Matti!

361
00:20:20,302 --> 00:20:24,306
You don't know how to swim.
Matti, like this.

362
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:26,725
Look at me! Rene!

363
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:29,061
-Matti!
-Matti!

364
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:30,103
My God!

365
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:33,148
[panting]

366
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:38,028
[distant voices]

367
00:20:44,284 --> 00:20:45,953
Jo. Hey, wait!

368
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,465
{\an8}Matti!

369
00:20:58,548 --> 00:21:00,092
[coughing]

370
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:02,344
[Paz] My God! Matti!

371
00:21:03,845 --> 00:21:04,972
Matti!

372
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:06,682
What the fuck were you thinking?

373
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:08,850
You can't swim.

374
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:11,061
You could have drowned out there!

375
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:13,313
You could have died out there! Stupid!

376
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:15,732
[Rene] Hey, relax, calm down.

377
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:18,568
You never listen to me.

378
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:19,945
If you'd listened to me,

379
00:21:20,028 --> 00:21:22,906
you can't fucking swim! Goddamn it!

380
00:21:24,616 --> 00:21:26,868
-You were told.
-[Rene] Hey, calm down!

381
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:28,620
He'll be all right on my watch.

382
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:30,455
What the hell? He could have died!

383
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:32,165
I'll give him swimming lessons.

384
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:34,167
I can't believe you all.

385
00:21:34,751 --> 00:21:36,128
Damn you! Modesta,

386
00:21:36,211 --> 00:21:38,130
I don't want to deal with my child!

387
00:21:38,213 --> 00:21:39,256
Now, come on.

388
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,841
-You!
-Stop that!

389
00:21:40,924 --> 00:21:43,510
-What's the matter with you?
-[Bes] That's enough now.

390
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:45,053
-Fuck!
-That's enough.

391
00:21:47,931 --> 00:21:50,892
[on radio] <i>I just need to buy medicine</i>
<i>for my mom.</i>

392
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:53,395
<i>She's been sick for a long time.</i>

393
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:56,940
<i>I have no other way of earning money.</i>

394
00:21:57,774 --> 00:21:59,109
<i>Have pity on me.</i>

395
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:04,865
Manang, don't you get sick
of these radio dramas?

396
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:09,202
<i>Please, please, have mercy on our port.</i>

397
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:11,288
[phone ringing]

398
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:17,002
Darling. Jo. Sweetheart, it's your phone.

399
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:20,380
-Mom?
-Here.

400
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:32,100
That's how she addresses you?

401
00:22:36,396 --> 00:22:37,314
Mmm.

402
00:22:43,111 --> 00:22:44,780
[counsellor] <i>Hi. Where are you?</i>

403
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:45,906
San Rafael.

404
00:22:45,989 --> 00:22:49,242
You went there. If you told me,
I would've come with you.

405
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:50,744
And why would you come here?

406
00:22:52,329 --> 00:22:53,580
Moral support.

407
00:22:53,663 --> 00:22:54,998
Are you okay?

408
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:55,999
Trying.

409
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:59,628
[Paz] Darling, the food's getting cold.

410
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:01,129
I gotta go.

411
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:02,089
Jo.

412
00:23:05,884 --> 00:23:07,636
You-hoo!

413
00:23:08,678 --> 00:23:10,013
Maria Paz?

414
00:23:11,598 --> 00:23:13,433
Maria Paz Del La Santos?

415
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:18,105
Paz, do you think that
you're going to be here for good?

416
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:22,109
Because, if you're here for good,
we should have a get together.

417
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:23,693
A party?

418
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:25,237
No, I'm too old.

419
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:26,696
Just a simple one.

420
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:28,740
Who would be there?

421
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:29,741
Relatives.

422
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:32,494
No.

423
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:33,620
Why not?

424
00:23:33,703 --> 00:23:35,539
All right. Just your brother then.

425
00:23:36,164 --> 00:23:38,959
And you could invite your friends
from showbiz, from the old days.

426
00:23:39,042 --> 00:23:43,213
Please invite them, especially…
I see her all the time on the television.

427
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:44,673
You were always together.

428
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:47,467
She's still very famous these days.

429
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:48,593
[whispers] Stella.

430
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:50,804
Stella, yes. Mmm.

431
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:51,805
Mmm.

432
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:55,016
I feel nervous all of a sudden.

433
00:23:56,351 --> 00:23:57,269
You know what?

434
00:23:58,311 --> 00:24:03,733
If your mother didn't go to the States,
she would have become a big star,

435
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:08,071
because way back then,
she acted with Cherie Hill…

436
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:11,449
-Mmm.
-with Gretchen, Alice Dixon,

437
00:24:12,075 --> 00:24:16,079
and the biggest star around,
Stella Guevara.

438
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:20,709
Very nice.

439
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:23,753
Where did you find this kid?

440
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:26,590
I'm not filling you in now, aunt,
maybe next time.

441
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:42,814
-I hate it here, Mom.
-Do you hear what you're saying?

442
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:43,982
Matti!

443
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:47,235
[Paz] Stop it.

444
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:50,113
Why did you bring me here?
I don't belong here.

445
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:53,533
[Paz] What are you doing?
You're gonna live off the streets?

446
00:24:54,117 --> 00:24:55,619
-[Matti groans]
-Oh, be quiet!

447
00:24:56,244 --> 00:24:58,705
I don't belong here.
Why did you bring me here?

448
00:24:58,788 --> 00:25:00,123
What happened to you there?

449
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:01,708
Matti!

450
00:25:01,791 --> 00:25:03,418
What? What are you gonna do?

451
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,004
You'll be on the street.

452
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:08,381
-You have nothing to go back…
-Don't touch me!

453
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,717
We have nothing to go back to there.

454
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,844
Maybe you, but not me!

455
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:15,305
Why does it always have to be <i>your</i> way?

456
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:17,098
You think your father will save you?

457
00:25:17,974 --> 00:25:19,517
Your dad's a coward.

458
00:25:20,101 --> 00:25:22,646
Yes, he wants nothing to do with you.

459
00:25:22,729 --> 00:25:24,981
-[Matti grunts]
-Come here. Stop it, Matti!

460
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:27,317
Matti, stop!

461
00:25:28,068 --> 00:25:29,361
Stop it!

462
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:30,362
Stop it!

463
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:31,905
Stop! Stop!

464
00:25:31,988 --> 00:25:32,906
Stop it!

465
00:25:32,989 --> 00:25:34,449
[Matti crying]

466
00:25:39,162 --> 00:25:41,206
I'm here. I'm here for you.

467
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:42,999
It's okay.

468
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:46,044
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay,

469
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:48,922
-it's okay, it's okay.
-[Matti sobbing]

470
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:12,612
And who's this?
Your partner in the movie?

471
00:26:13,863 --> 00:26:16,616
{\an8}Yes, Kenneth. Look at his bulge.

472
00:26:17,284 --> 00:26:19,160
{\an8}Looks like a child's arm.

473
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:22,831
They used to wrap it up in a stocking.

474
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:24,124
That's how it was done.

475
00:26:29,838 --> 00:26:30,755
My goodness.

476
00:26:32,048 --> 00:26:32,924
Look,

477
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:34,968
this is old.

478
00:26:35,051 --> 00:26:36,428
What's this doing out here?

479
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,474
You look, you're so young there.

480
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:43,101
Look, there's Joanne.

481
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:47,314
Yeah, where was that?

482
00:26:47,397 --> 00:26:49,482
It was in La Union.

483
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:51,234
[Bes] Jo, darling.

484
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:54,779
Joanne, come look.

485
00:26:56,906 --> 00:26:57,824
Look.

486
00:26:58,491 --> 00:27:00,285
Modesta when she was younger.

487
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:04,789
And look at you.

488
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:06,750
We have no pictures together.

489
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:09,753
I'm always with Nono and Nana.

490
00:27:12,547 --> 00:27:13,631
You were never there.

491
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:18,678
See.

492
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:22,515
-Will I bring this out?
-Mm.

493
00:27:33,568 --> 00:27:35,320
Who do you think took the pictures?

494
00:27:41,576 --> 00:27:42,494
[sneezes]

495
00:27:44,662 --> 00:27:48,166
Modesta, you need to clean in here.

496
00:27:53,171 --> 00:27:54,214
Time to sing.

497
00:27:54,297 --> 00:27:55,382
You ready for karaoke?

498
00:27:56,132 --> 00:27:57,300
What?

499
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:58,551
-What is that?
-Hey, Paz.

500
00:27:59,260 --> 00:28:01,429
-Rene! Whose idea was this?
-What?

501
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:04,349
-I thought you wanted some sound.
-Music.

502
00:28:04,432 --> 00:28:06,810
This is loud noise. Just loud noise.

503
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:10,188
It's all the same, right?
This is hard to wrangle.

504
00:28:10,271 --> 00:28:11,648
All right, boys, lets…

505
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:13,483
You're such a ridiculous man.

506
00:28:13,566 --> 00:28:15,485
Sounds, all right, sounds!

507
00:28:15,568 --> 00:28:18,655
This is a terrible idea!

508
00:28:18,738 --> 00:28:20,532
Come on, boys, put it here.

509
00:28:20,615 --> 00:28:21,825
What have I forgotten?

510
00:28:21,908 --> 00:28:23,535
Ice! Ice!

511
00:28:23,618 --> 00:28:24,702
You already did that.

512
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:27,247
Well, they already got ice.
It's done.

513
00:28:27,330 --> 00:28:28,373
What else is there?

514
00:28:30,708 --> 00:28:32,210
Everyone here! They've arrived.

515
00:28:34,587 --> 00:28:38,091
-[music playing]
-[indistinct chatter]

516
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:42,846
[Paz] <i>Your dad's a coward!</i>

517
00:28:47,058 --> 00:28:47,976
<i>Goddamn!</i>

518
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:49,936
<i>Matti.</i>

519
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:52,689
[music continues]

520
00:29:00,697 --> 00:29:02,782
[remembering Paz's conversation]

521
00:29:04,117 --> 00:29:05,201
<i>Your dad's a coward.</i>

522
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:07,829
<i>He's a coward. A coward.</i>

523
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:15,128
[Rene] Come here! Hey, come out!

524
00:29:15,211 --> 00:29:19,507
Everyone, they're here! Hey, hey!

525
00:29:20,550 --> 00:29:22,218
