Thank you. Thank you.

782
00:41:08,090 --> 00:41:09,383
<i>Okay. Bye.</i>

783
00:41:12,511 --> 00:41:15,389
[Skype ringtone]

784
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:18,017
-Hi, Ben.
-[Ben] <i>What's up, Jo?</i>

785
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:21,729
-I'm in.
<i>-Ah, that's awesome news.</i>

786
00:41:21,812 --> 00:41:23,147
<i>Just in time.</i>

787
00:41:23,230 --> 00:41:27,109
<i>I was talking to Mike the other day</i>
<i>and he thinks your pitch has promise.</i>

788
00:41:27,193 --> 00:41:29,236
<i>And when Mike says</i>
<i>something like that, you're in.</i>

789
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:31,322
<i>Now finish that treatment.</i>

790
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:33,115
I will.

791
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:37,161
What was it called?

792
00:41:38,329 --> 00:41:40,539
<i>-Proud Wizards.</i>
-[Pipo] You're grinning from ear to ear.

793
00:41:40,623 --> 00:41:42,249
Hey, what… What have you heard?

794
00:41:43,667 --> 00:41:44,877
-What's up?
-[Paz] What is it?

795
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,712
-What?
-[Paz] What is it?

796
00:41:47,463 --> 00:41:48,714
What is it?

797
00:41:48,797 --> 00:41:50,007
Did you find out?

798
00:41:51,675 --> 00:41:54,178
-[grunts]
-Wait. Finally.

799
00:41:54,261 --> 00:41:57,306
-Yes, Uncle.
-Oh, my God, yes! The States!

800
00:41:57,389 --> 00:42:00,017
-The suspense. Now I wanna know.
-[Pipo] Congrats! Oh, my God!

801
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:02,353
She got accepted
for a screenwriting fellowship.

802
00:42:03,187 --> 00:42:06,106
A very prestigious one.
It's a really big one.

803
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:09,818
-Congratulations!
-All right!

804
00:42:09,902 --> 00:42:12,363
-I'm so happy for you.
-Thank you.

805
00:42:12,446 --> 00:42:13,656
What, you're leaving?

806
00:42:15,032 --> 00:42:15,991
For where?

807
00:42:16,075 --> 00:42:17,451
Brooklyn.

808
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:18,452
Oh, New York.

809
00:42:19,245 --> 00:42:20,162
How'd you get that?

810
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:26,210
An agent friend told me about it
so I applied for it, and I got in.

811
00:42:26,293 --> 00:42:28,712
It's pretty clear
where you got your talent.

812
00:42:28,796 --> 00:42:31,173
That's amazing.
When do you leave?

813
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:33,467
[both] Next month.

814
00:42:34,843 --> 00:42:35,761
Uh…

815
00:42:37,388 --> 00:42:38,389
I'm really proud of her.

816
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:42,101
She worked hard for this,
and she's very humble about it.

817
00:42:43,561 --> 00:42:44,770
Whose child are…

818
00:42:45,479 --> 00:42:47,523
-Uh, you're asking…
-Aunt, he's a friend of mine.

819
00:42:47,606 --> 00:42:48,566
-Uh, a friend.
-Ah.

820
00:42:49,525 --> 00:42:51,235
And what job do you do?

821
00:42:51,318 --> 00:42:52,987
I'm a psychiatrist.

822
00:42:53,070 --> 00:42:54,321
Psychiatrist.

823
00:42:55,072 --> 00:42:57,032
[Stella] Ah. You're a doctor?

824
00:42:57,116 --> 00:43:00,995
Yes. Yes, I am focusing
on psychosomatic psychiatry.

825
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:02,538
[Tita Abby] Very fancy.

826
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:07,167
Hey, come and have dinner with us, Tito!

827
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:09,878
Eat something before you drink too much.

828
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:12,423
-Come in, Tito.
-… is that my uncle?

829
00:43:13,757 --> 00:43:14,925
He hasn't changed at all.

830
00:43:15,009 --> 00:43:16,260
-Hi.
-…the pity.

831
00:43:17,303 --> 00:43:19,054
-Hi!
-[Tito] Hello.

832
00:43:20,514 --> 00:43:21,390
Are you good?

833
00:43:22,016 --> 00:43:23,934
-[Tita Abby] Oh, Lord.
-What's this?

834
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:26,228
Lechon.

835
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:28,522
It's full of fat. Eat lots of it.

836
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:30,065
Maybe you'll die fast.

837
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:31,400
-[Stella laughs]
-You're sweet.

838
00:43:31,483 --> 00:43:34,111
-This man.
-[Tito] It's good. Have some.

839
00:43:34,194 --> 00:43:36,572
[Tita Abby] Stop leaning on me.
I hate that

840
00:43:36,655 --> 00:43:37,698
That wasn't as big before.

841
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:38,657
Before?

842
00:43:40,242 --> 00:43:42,953
-You never came here to visit Papa.
-[Pipo] Oh, come on.

843
00:43:43,037 --> 00:43:45,331
You didn't have enough room
for both of us.

844
00:43:45,414 --> 00:43:47,333
-You're an idiot, you know?
-Look who's talking.

845
00:43:47,416 --> 00:43:49,627
Hey, psst, enough already.

846
00:43:49,710 --> 00:43:51,670
Your father was a good person.

847
00:43:51,754 --> 00:43:53,213
-That'll do.
-That's true.

848
00:43:53,922 --> 00:43:56,925
Your dad was really good
to the chicks. [grunts]

849
00:43:57,009 --> 00:43:59,261
[laughs] Right?

850
00:43:59,345 --> 00:44:03,599
-Hey, I won't hear any of this!
-[Tito] Yes, sir.

851
00:44:05,225 --> 00:44:07,436
-What?
-What? What is it?

852
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:09,813
Papa was a depressed man.

853
00:44:09,897 --> 00:44:10,856
He wasn't depressed.

854
00:44:11,690 --> 00:44:13,150
The doctors just made that up.

855
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:18,113
[Migs] Uh, sorry.

856
00:44:18,989 --> 00:44:22,117
Depression is actually
a medical condition,

857
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:23,827
believe it or not.

858
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:25,788
It's a mental disorder.

859
00:44:25,871 --> 00:44:26,747
Migs.

860
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:28,999
-[mouthing]
-That's bullshit.

861
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,543
It didn't exist before.

862
00:44:31,627 --> 00:44:37,216
[chuckles] Well, the good news is that
our holy prayers can fix everything.

863
00:44:37,299 --> 00:44:40,636
-That's right. Correct.
-All we need to do is just pray.

864
00:44:41,303 --> 00:44:43,847
Now there are faith healers
everywhere you look,

865
00:44:44,556 --> 00:44:46,558
[chuckling] using herbs to clear the head.

866
00:44:46,642 --> 00:44:48,936
[all chuckling]

867
00:44:49,019 --> 00:44:50,062
Isn't that right?

868
00:44:51,146 --> 00:44:53,607
-Praying can be beneficial.
-Uh-huh.

869
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:58,904
Usually, anxiety and depression
are natural responses

870
00:44:58,987 --> 00:45:00,697
to life's circumstances.

871
00:45:01,698 --> 00:45:03,242
You know, when you lose your job,

872
00:45:03,325 --> 00:45:05,536
or when you're grieving,

873
00:45:06,412 --> 00:45:09,415
or sometimes, when a loved one goes away.

874
00:45:10,082 --> 00:45:11,875
And you're right.

875
00:45:11,959 --> 00:45:13,710
Prayer can be a source of hope.

876
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:15,546
-Mmm.
-…yeah.

877
00:45:15,629 --> 00:45:19,550
However, there are some times,
even when you pray, that the heaviness

878
00:45:20,092 --> 00:45:21,718
and the pain doesn't go away.

879
00:45:21,802 --> 00:45:24,179
Or worse, the more you live with it,

880
00:45:24,263 --> 00:45:27,724
the heaviness increases
and you can't deal with it anymore.

881
00:45:27,808 --> 00:45:28,934
[Tita Abby] Mmm.

882
00:45:29,017 --> 00:45:32,396
When that happens,
that means it's too big.

883
00:45:33,063 --> 00:45:35,065
-Ohh.
-That's when you see a specialist.

884
00:45:35,649 --> 00:45:37,693
That's what you're good at, Doctor.

885
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:40,320
Selling drugs.

886
00:45:40,946 --> 00:45:42,698
Happiness isn't so hard.

887
00:45:43,240 --> 00:45:45,367
-[Rene laughs]
-Have a beer, right, Rene?

888
00:45:46,535 --> 00:45:47,578
Buddy?

889
00:45:47,661 --> 00:45:50,914
Singing karaoke,
cockfighting, cards. Yes.

890
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:56,003
There's lots of ways
to be merry. Lots.

891
00:45:57,129 --> 00:46:00,924
But if someone's gone completely crazy,
put them in the nuthouse.

892
00:46:01,008 --> 00:46:02,551
[laughs]

893
00:46:02,634 --> 00:46:04,011
[coughs]

894
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:05,846
Uncle, drink. Drink some water.

895
00:46:05,929 --> 00:46:07,306
[Tita Abby] Don't throw up here!

896
00:46:07,389 --> 00:46:09,558
Hey, hey! Don't throw up here!

897
00:46:09,641 --> 00:46:12,269
This is exactly why people
take their own lives.

898
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:13,353
Among other things.

899
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:16,148
-[Tita Abby] Go outside!
-Stop it, Matti.

900
00:46:16,231 --> 00:46:17,524
[Tita Abby] Outside now!

901
00:46:18,358 --> 00:46:20,652
-Get your act together.
-I will. Don't you worry.

902
00:46:22,112 --> 00:46:22,988
There you go.

903
00:46:23,947 --> 00:46:25,949
-That's why you need faith.
-[Stella laughs]

904
00:46:26,033 --> 00:46:30,162
<i>I dedicate this song</i>
<i>to all the women I've loved before.</i>

905
00:46:35,792 --> 00:46:38,378
I think you need to get your son examined.

906
00:46:39,922 --> 00:46:41,798
[Paz] Oh, my goodness, Aunt,

907
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:46,303
I hear all kinds of noises
when he is on his own day and night,

908
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:48,180
not to mention that he paces

909
00:46:48,847 --> 00:46:50,766
all the time. Plays music loudly.

910
00:46:50,849 --> 00:46:52,851
I'm tired and I'm exhausted.

911
00:46:53,644 --> 00:46:55,229
What are you telling her for?

912
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:58,649
Oh, I was just telling her
that you're an artist like me.

913
00:46:58,732 --> 00:47:00,817
Oh, come on. Just for once,
be honest with them.

914
00:47:00,901 --> 00:47:04,279
Tell them your son is depressed,
bipolar, manic depressive.

915
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,656
Why are you so ashamed of me?

916
00:47:06,573 --> 00:47:08,158
And tell them that you hear voices.

917
00:47:11,328 --> 00:47:15,123
And you have flashes of horrible memories
and you feel abandoned by your dad,

918
00:47:15,207 --> 00:47:17,584
and can't calm down
without your fucking weed or your Xanax.

919
00:47:17,668 --> 00:47:20,963
-Just let it out just a minute.
-He's just created this out of nothing.

920
00:47:21,046 --> 00:47:22,923
This kid lies a lot.

921
00:47:23,715 --> 00:47:26,218
Imagine, I've had to put up
with this for 20 years!

922
00:47:27,302 --> 00:47:29,972
Do you have any idea if he's…

923
00:47:30,055 --> 00:47:31,265
Can you shut the fuck up?

924
00:47:31,348 --> 00:47:32,391
Ah!

925
00:47:32,474 --> 00:47:34,101
You wanna know where my father is?

926
00:47:34,184 --> 00:47:37,479
I can't tell you where my father is.
I have no idea.

927
00:47:37,563 --> 00:47:40,607
Maybe he's in jail,
or maybe he's dead, or drunk somewhere.

928
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:43,735
Or worse, with a happy family.
He doesn't acknowledge that I exist.

929
00:47:44,403 --> 00:47:47,614
And my mom just eats all that shit up
because she's being paid handsomely.

930
00:47:47,698 --> 00:47:49,741
And at whose expense? Mine!

931
00:47:49,825 --> 00:47:51,451
[grunting]

932
00:47:51,535 --> 00:47:52,578
Any more questions?

933
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:55,038
You son of a bitch!

934
00:47:55,122 --> 00:47:56,957
Huh? You're a fucking ass!

935
00:47:57,708 --> 00:48:00,210
After all I've been through for you,
this is what I get?

936
00:48:01,169 --> 00:48:05,299
You don't understand a fucking thing,
you ungrateful piece of shit.

937
00:48:06,216 --> 00:48:09,094
How do you think we managed
to make it through day by day

938
00:48:09,177 --> 00:48:12,723
if I didn't eat shit for you?
That was all for you, Matti.

939
00:48:13,807 --> 00:48:16,226
Huh? Where would you be without me?

940
00:48:16,310 --> 00:48:18,520
And you want to go back to America? Huh?

941
00:48:18,604 --> 00:48:21,148
Go ahead! See if you'll be able
to live for just…

942
00:48:21,231 --> 00:48:22,816
You can't even fucking swim!

943
00:48:22,899 --> 00:48:24,484
Do you have to talk to him that way?

944
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:30,032
Oh! Here we are!
Going through the laundry basket. Oh.

945
00:48:30,616 --> 00:48:32,075
Don't leave… Stay.

946
00:48:32,159 --> 00:48:33,702
I don't want you to miss a thing.

947
00:48:35,370 --> 00:48:39,416
That's what you're all here for, right?
To chew on every bit of shit.

948
00:48:40,417 --> 00:48:41,585
Hey, Aunt Abby.

949
00:48:42,669 --> 00:48:45,881
Do you really want to know
why I came back? Huh?

950
00:48:47,049 --> 00:48:48,258
You can't wait to hear.

951
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:54,389
Fuck this. Goddamn it!

952
00:49:05,484 --> 00:49:07,069
What did she go and do that for?

953
00:49:09,071 --> 00:49:10,072
[sighs]

954
00:49:16,328 --> 00:49:17,287
I have cancer.

955
00:49:21,583 --> 00:49:22,626
I've come home to die.

956
00:49:26,922 --> 00:49:28,173
Ugh.

957
00:49:34,596 --> 00:49:35,514
[sighs]

958
00:49:44,398 --> 00:49:45,399
Lighter, please.

959
00:50:28,692 --> 00:50:29,651
Want to smoke?

960
00:50:32,571 --> 00:50:33,447
It's okay.

961
00:50:40,954 --> 00:50:43,415
That was a crazy scene you made in there.

962
00:50:46,585 --> 00:50:47,919
I didn't start it.

963
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:55,135
How long have you known?

964
00:50:57,763 --> 00:50:58,764
About a year now.

965
00:51:03,560 --> 00:51:04,811
And what stage?

966
00:51:07,689 --> 00:51:09,274
-End stage.
-What?

967
00:51:14,613 --> 00:51:15,489
Chemo?

968
00:51:16,156 --> 00:51:18,658
-Are you considering chemo?
-[sighs]

969
00:51:19,284 --> 00:51:20,202
I tried it.

970
00:51:21,203 --> 00:51:25,332
It just makes me feel sicker. Hmm?

971
00:51:32,172 --> 00:51:34,216
But this, oh,

972
00:51:36,927 --> 00:51:38,094
makes me feel better.

973
00:51:40,680 --> 00:51:43,308
[Stella laughs, sighs]

974
00:51:49,981 --> 00:51:53,443
You're going to outlast me again,
aren't you, you witch?

975
00:51:54,110 --> 00:51:55,612
[both chuckle]

976
00:51:57,447 --> 00:51:58,448
Paz.

977
00:52:01,493 --> 00:52:05,330
I hope you know that I sincerely,

978
00:52:05,413 --> 00:52:07,582
genuinely look up to you.

979
00:52:09,417 --> 00:52:13,046
Ugh. You make me sound old. Stop that.

980
00:52:13,129 --> 00:52:14,256
I'm serious, though.

981
00:52:17,008 --> 00:52:18,134
Look at you.

982
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:20,428
You go for what you want.

983
00:52:21,721 --> 00:52:25,433
No apologies. Without caring
what other people think.

984
00:52:26,142 --> 00:52:28,270
I wish I could be like that--

985
00:52:28,353 --> 00:52:31,982
Hey, wait. You're living your dream.

986
00:52:33,108 --> 00:52:34,901
Me? Look at me.

987
00:52:35,402 --> 00:52:37,404
I'm a sick old lady dying of cancer.

988
00:52:38,905 --> 00:52:40,365
What are you talking about?

989
00:52:41,366 --> 00:52:42,284
What is this?

990
00:52:43,243 --> 00:52:45,871
You're making films in America.

991
00:52:45,954 --> 00:52:47,497
That's every actor's dream.

992
00:52:47,581 --> 00:52:48,498
I did one.

993
00:52:49,541 --> 00:52:50,542
Even then I blew it.

994
00:52:52,252 --> 00:52:54,671
You heard Matti.
I punched the director.

995
00:52:58,466 --> 00:52:59,551
Did he harass you?

996
00:53:04,681 --> 00:53:07,142
[exhales]

997
00:53:10,186 --> 00:53:11,438
[groans]

998
00:53:11,521 --> 00:53:12,397
Are you okay?

999
00:53:14,649 --> 00:53:15,567
Hey,

1000
00:53:16,568 --> 00:53:17,402
Paz.

1001
00:53:21,156 --> 00:53:23,241
Why do bad things happen to good people?

1002
00:53:29,539 --> 00:53:31,833
-[laughs]
-What are you laughing about?

1003
00:53:31,917 --> 00:53:35,587
I never thought I'd be
hearing you talk like that.

1004
00:53:36,588 --> 00:53:38,840
{\an8}[Paz] Wow, you're so mean.

1005
00:53:40,091 --> 00:53:41,384
{\an8}Here, give me that.

1006
00:53:50,602 --> 00:53:52,854
[cell phone ringing]

1007
00:54:26,554 --> 00:54:28,890
[birds chirping]

1008
00:55:32,454 --> 00:55:34,873
[Paz] …we don't have any water.

1009
00:55:34,956 --> 00:55:36,082
Well, hello.

1010
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,167
Yes, thank you.

1011
00:55:37,917 --> 00:55:38,835
[Paz] There's Miguel.

1012
00:55:39,878 --> 00:55:41,254
Hi. Good morning.

1013
00:55:41,337 --> 00:55:43,131
[Pipo] Here you go. This is delicious.

1014
00:55:45,467 --> 00:55:47,427
-[Jo] Morning.
-Morning.

1015
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:50,180
No, I'm okay. Thank you.

1016
00:55:56,061 --> 00:55:57,187
Where did you go?

1017
00:55:57,270 --> 00:55:58,521
Out for a drive.

1018
00:56:01,983 --> 00:56:02,901
I was alone.

1019
00:56:05,612 --> 00:56:07,655
Did I ask you to come here, Migs?

1020
00:56:13,620 --> 00:56:14,537
Have some food.

1021
00:56:14,621 --> 00:56:15,789
No, I don't feel…

1022
00:56:17,290 --> 00:56:18,374
Uh, there. Thank you.

1023
00:56:22,754 --> 00:56:24,339
We need to visit the doctor.

1024
00:56:25,548 --> 00:56:26,466
Why?

1025
00:56:27,467 --> 00:56:28,384
Are you sick?

1026
00:56:28,468 --> 00:56:29,761
It's for you.

1027
00:56:29,844 --> 00:56:30,720
Ugh.

1028
00:56:32,514 --> 00:56:34,808
Don't go there, Joanne.

1029
00:56:35,683 --> 00:56:38,686
-I think we need to know about--
-To know about what?

1030
00:56:38,770 --> 00:56:41,064
-If I have longer?
-So we're fully informed.

1031
00:56:41,815 --> 00:56:43,191
Who's asking you?

1032
00:56:44,109 --> 00:56:45,360
This is my decision, right?

1033
00:56:46,277 --> 00:56:47,445
I'll take care of myself.

1034
00:56:48,655 --> 00:56:51,741
So for now, I'm just gonna sit
and wait it out until I croak.

1035
00:56:52,951 --> 00:56:55,912
… come on, sit down
and join us. Relax.

1036
00:56:55,995 --> 00:56:57,747
Why don't you want to be checked?

1037
00:56:58,748 --> 00:57:00,208
There's nothing to lose, right?

1038
00:57:01,042 --> 00:57:01,960
You as well.

1039
00:57:04,546 --> 00:57:07,048
You know what?
I'm sick and tired of doctors

1040
00:57:07,549 --> 00:57:10,969
and the smell of hospitals,
so please, huh, let me be.

1041
00:57:14,806 --> 00:57:16,558
How do we know you're not making this up?

1042
00:57:19,477 --> 00:57:20,937
Fucking unbelievable.

1043
00:57:28,736 --> 00:57:29,654
[Jo clears throat]

1044
00:57:33,158 --> 00:57:34,325
You don't believe me, huh?

1045
00:57:35,785 --> 00:57:36,995
You need proof?

1046
00:57:37,620 --> 00:57:38,538
Okay.

1047
00:57:39,456 --> 00:57:40,331
Here.

1048
00:57:42,167 --> 00:57:43,877
