1246
01:12:58,415 --> 01:13:01,335
Oh. I'm the stubborn one. [chuckles]

1247
01:13:02,836 --> 01:13:03,754
Wow.

1248
01:13:07,841 --> 01:13:10,094
I tried reaching out to her, you know.

1249
01:13:10,177 --> 01:13:13,013
I sent emails, I never got a reply.

1250
01:13:14,098 --> 01:13:15,265
So I eventually gave up.

1251
01:13:21,688 --> 01:13:22,523
Oh.

1252
01:13:23,816 --> 01:13:25,818
Okay, I'm good. It's all good.

1253
01:13:35,744 --> 01:13:36,662
[Matti giggles]

1254
01:13:36,745 --> 01:13:37,704
[Jo] Good Lord.

1255
01:13:43,961 --> 01:13:47,047
Okay, just remember,
if you're in deep water,

1256
01:13:47,714 --> 01:13:48,632
head first.

1257
01:13:49,174 --> 01:13:54,263
And after that, you do the frog kick,
you know, like that, huh?

1258
01:13:55,514 --> 01:13:56,640
And then you'll stay afloat.

1259
01:13:57,266 --> 01:13:59,726
Yeah? Come on, you'll learn.

1260
01:14:00,894 --> 01:14:01,895
Tanchi!

1261
01:14:02,563 --> 01:14:04,815
It's a swimming lesson,
so take us to the island.

1262
01:14:07,484 --> 01:14:10,154
You know, you're a really cool dad.

1263
01:14:11,113 --> 01:14:13,031
You're a crazy boy, you know that?

1264
01:14:13,115 --> 01:14:16,118
No, I really mean it. I think
I'm gonna call you pops from now on.

1265
01:14:17,619 --> 01:14:19,538
[both chuckle]

1266
01:14:19,621 --> 01:14:22,291
Let's go! Okay…

1267
01:14:22,374 --> 01:14:24,084
one, two, three!

1268
01:14:25,377 --> 01:14:27,129
[boat engine whirring]

1269
01:14:39,641 --> 01:14:41,477
[fish vocal sounds]

1270
01:15:09,922 --> 01:15:11,215
How's your script?

1271
01:15:14,301 --> 01:15:15,302
It's all right.

1272
01:15:18,347 --> 01:15:19,765
Writers block?

1273
01:15:21,058 --> 01:15:22,226
[clears throat]

1274
01:15:24,853 --> 01:15:27,856
I'm stuck because I don't know

1275
01:15:27,940 --> 01:15:29,441
how to end it.

1276
01:15:32,694 --> 01:15:34,279
Do you have to know the ending?

1277
01:15:37,616 --> 01:15:40,035
I want to know where it's going.

1278
01:15:40,118 --> 01:15:42,538
Well, what a corny approach.

1279
01:15:45,332 --> 01:15:47,501
So, writing feels like…

1280
01:15:48,085 --> 01:15:52,381
like a to-do list
when it's really, you know, an experience.

1281
01:15:55,175 --> 01:15:56,009
I don't know…

1282
01:15:57,344 --> 01:15:59,137
you don't have to have just one ending.

1283
01:16:00,973 --> 01:16:02,599
I don't know, just…

1284
01:16:04,601 --> 01:16:06,103
go with the flow,

1285
01:16:07,187 --> 01:16:09,731
and just feel every scene.

1286
01:16:11,775 --> 01:16:13,902
And see where it takes you.

1287
01:16:22,911 --> 01:16:24,329
Do you remember Nono?

1288
01:16:28,458 --> 01:16:29,626
Yeah.

1289
01:16:32,462 --> 01:16:36,341
Every night, he would put on an LP

1290
01:16:36,425 --> 01:16:38,427
while I put you to sleep.

1291
01:16:40,762 --> 01:16:45,017
I always remember that he had a laugh
like Donald Duck.

1292
01:16:46,143 --> 01:16:47,644
[mimics laugh]

1293
01:16:49,062 --> 01:16:50,147
[chuckles]

1294
01:16:58,322 --> 01:17:01,575
He was a brilliant, brilliant lawyer…

1295
01:17:03,744 --> 01:17:05,621
and also a very good writer.

1296
01:17:08,081 --> 01:17:10,042
If only I knew then what I know now.

1297
01:17:14,087 --> 01:17:16,298
You know, I could've…

1298
01:17:24,431 --> 01:17:26,224
he called you princess.

1299
01:17:26,308 --> 01:17:27,392
Do you remember that?

1300
01:17:33,065 --> 01:17:35,108
He must be so proud of you now, Jo.

1301
01:17:50,540 --> 01:17:52,459
[Matti] Come on, mom,
you're gonna love it!

1302
01:17:52,542 --> 01:17:54,002
Come on out!

1303
01:17:54,086 --> 01:17:56,254
Your son wants you to join us!

1304
01:17:56,338 --> 01:17:57,506
[both chuckle]

1305
01:18:02,052 --> 01:18:03,845
[engine whirring]

1306
01:18:09,101 --> 01:18:11,353
[cheerful screams]

1307
01:18:45,929 --> 01:18:48,390
Paz, drink something,
then you'll feel better.

1308
01:18:48,473 --> 01:18:49,683
Thanks.

1309
01:18:50,726 --> 01:18:52,769
Let's take a family picture.

1310
01:18:53,687 --> 01:18:55,105
Yeah, let's do it.

1311
01:18:55,188 --> 01:18:56,481
-Ma!
-What?

1312
01:18:56,565 --> 01:18:59,067
-Please take our picture. Mm-hmm.
-I just have to click it?

1313
01:18:59,151 --> 01:19:01,111
-You're drinking beer again?
-Just the one.

1314
01:19:01,194 --> 01:19:02,738
Everyone look happy, all right?

1315
01:19:04,614 --> 01:19:05,949
Over here!

1316
01:19:06,032 --> 01:19:07,951
Okay, um…

1317
01:19:09,453 --> 01:19:11,204
[Joe] Mom, you have to count.

1318
01:19:11,288 --> 01:19:13,331
Count, then click.

1319
01:19:13,415 --> 01:19:17,085
Okay, one, two, three, four five…

1320
01:19:17,169 --> 01:19:18,587
-What!
-Hey!

1321
01:19:19,546 --> 01:19:22,215
One, two, three… one, two, three…

1322
01:19:22,299 --> 01:19:23,967
-[both] click!
-There you go.

1323
01:19:24,050 --> 01:19:26,720
Ah! Yeah!

1324
01:19:26,803 --> 01:19:27,929
Smile!

1325
01:19:28,013 --> 01:19:31,057
One, two, three, click!

1326
01:19:31,141 --> 01:19:34,269
There. Beautiful. One, two, three…
[camera shutter clicks]

1327
01:19:34,352 --> 01:19:36,271
Oh, wonderful!

1328
01:19:36,354 --> 01:19:38,273
One, two, three, click!

1329
01:19:38,774 --> 01:19:40,650
[all laughing]

1330
01:19:53,288 --> 01:19:54,998
[scoffs] It really hurts.

1331
01:19:59,336 --> 01:20:00,420
[gasps]

1332
01:20:08,678 --> 01:20:10,388
Will you marry the doctor?

1333
01:20:12,265 --> 01:20:14,017
I can have a doctor in the house.

1334
01:20:16,311 --> 01:20:18,188
Ma, he's just a friend.

1335
01:20:20,732 --> 01:20:21,942
I'm not stupid.

1336
01:20:23,527 --> 01:20:25,028
Just rest please.

1337
01:20:26,488 --> 01:20:27,948
How did you even meet?

1338
01:20:29,699 --> 01:20:30,909
Are you his patient?

1339
01:20:34,704 --> 01:20:35,914
Busted.

1340
01:20:37,666 --> 01:20:38,792
[chuckles softly]

1341
01:20:42,504 --> 01:20:44,214
I'm not judging you, Jo.

1342
01:20:45,382 --> 01:20:48,093
I've fucked a few doctors in my life.

1343
01:20:52,138 --> 01:20:53,431
Just be careful.

1344
01:21:00,522 --> 01:21:01,773
[exhales]

1345
01:21:06,236 --> 01:21:07,487
[groans softly]

1346
01:21:13,702 --> 01:21:14,703
[groans softly]

1347
01:21:27,549 --> 01:21:28,717
Ma?

1348
01:21:29,885 --> 01:21:31,803
[groans softly]

1349
01:21:31,887 --> 01:21:35,015
[groaning]

1350
01:21:35,557 --> 01:21:36,600
Mom.

1351
01:22:13,219 --> 01:22:14,971
[Ben] <i>Hey, what's wrong, Joe?</i>

1352
01:22:15,555 --> 01:22:18,391
<i>You've been hard to reach lately.</i>
<i>Everything all right?</i>

1353
01:22:18,475 --> 01:22:21,770
I'm sorry, Ben, I've been looking after
my sick mother.

1354
01:22:22,395 --> 01:22:25,148
<i>Aww, I'm sorry to hear that.</i>

1355
01:22:26,024 --> 01:22:27,442
<i>You should have said something.</i>

1356
01:22:28,109 --> 01:22:30,487
<i>You still wanna be a part of this, though?</i>

1357
01:22:31,154 --> 01:22:34,115
I've worked so hard for this, Ben.

1358
01:22:34,199 --> 01:22:35,325
<i>Oh…</i>

1359
01:22:36,117 --> 01:22:37,452
What should I do?

1360
01:22:38,453 --> 01:22:41,289
<i>I could try talking to</i>
<i>a few of my colleagues…</i>

1361
01:22:41,831 --> 01:22:43,291
-Ben…
<i>-Yeah?</i>

1362
01:22:43,375 --> 01:22:46,044
-I'm sorry but I gotta go.
<i>-You know what, Joe--</i>

1363
01:22:46,127 --> 01:22:48,046
[Rene] Pancit, everyone!

1364
01:22:48,129 --> 01:22:50,256
So delicious.

1365
01:22:50,340 --> 01:22:51,758
There we are.

1366
01:22:52,550 --> 01:22:54,177
[chuckles]

1367
01:22:54,260 --> 01:22:55,303
Hand me that.

1368
01:22:59,849 --> 01:23:01,559
-[Paz] Where is it, Rene?
-Here, it's here.

1369
01:23:04,270 --> 01:23:06,523
-Wow, thank you.
-That's okay.

1370
01:23:07,482 --> 01:23:08,692
Hand it to your sister.

1371
01:23:09,317 --> 01:23:11,069
[Bes] Pass your plate.

1372
01:23:13,613 --> 01:23:15,740
-Your sister. Give it to your sister.
-Right, right.

1373
01:23:15,824 --> 01:23:16,866
-Your sister.
-Here it is.

1374
01:23:16,950 --> 01:23:18,284
Uh, no.

1375
01:23:18,368 --> 01:23:19,953
I'm sorry. I have to work.

1376
01:23:20,036 --> 01:23:22,622
Come on, Jo. For me, please.

1377
01:23:22,706 --> 01:23:24,874
-[Matti] It's good.
-All right.

1378
01:23:24,958 --> 01:23:26,292
-[Bes] This is yours.
-Thanks.

1379
01:23:26,376 --> 01:23:29,421
-Come on.
-[Rene] Oh, yeah.

1380
01:23:30,630 --> 01:23:32,215
[puffs]

1381
01:23:34,634 --> 01:23:37,303
[coughs, chuckles]

1382
01:23:47,188 --> 01:23:48,481
[Bes] Take it easy.

1383
01:23:53,486 --> 01:23:54,863
Hey, slow down.

1384
01:23:55,405 --> 01:23:56,656
It's sumptuous.

1385
01:23:57,532 --> 01:23:58,867
[all chuckling]

1386
01:24:00,201 --> 01:24:02,829
[Bes] Do it. Please.
You'll end up choaking.

1387
01:24:05,165 --> 01:24:07,751
Mom, how is it?

1388
01:24:07,834 --> 01:24:09,335
The food.

1389
01:24:11,463 --> 01:24:13,423
This is perfect last meal.

1390
01:24:16,134 --> 01:24:17,677
-What?
-[Rene] Now, this is perfect.

1391
01:24:17,761 --> 01:24:19,220
You never know, right?

1392
01:24:19,971 --> 01:24:21,181
Mom!

1393
01:24:21,723 --> 01:24:23,767
-Just eat up.
-Ah-ha!

1394
01:24:23,850 --> 01:24:25,977
You guys are so not ready for this.

1395
01:24:28,396 --> 01:24:32,150
Have you guys thought of the eulogies
you're gonna give when I go?

1396
01:24:37,572 --> 01:24:38,615
Matti boy?

1397
01:24:39,657 --> 01:24:41,951
Come on, pretend that it's my funeral.

1398
01:24:42,035 --> 01:24:44,454
-You have to say something.
-I don't wanna do that, mom.

1399
01:24:44,537 --> 01:24:46,539
Just try it, Matias.

1400
01:24:46,623 --> 01:24:47,999
Try!

1401
01:24:48,083 --> 01:24:50,251
-Come on, you can do this.
-All right, all right.

1402
01:24:51,044 --> 01:24:54,506
Everybody, thank you for coming tonight.

1403
01:24:54,589 --> 01:24:56,341
I'm so fucked faded right now.

1404
01:24:56,424 --> 01:24:58,176
[all chuckling]

1405
01:24:59,719 --> 01:25:02,097
Tonight, my dear mother…

1406
01:25:03,264 --> 01:25:05,058
is dead.

1407
01:25:05,141 --> 01:25:07,060
[all chuckle]

1408
01:25:10,271 --> 01:25:12,565
Matti, come on.

1409
01:25:12,649 --> 01:25:14,609
Jesus, Mary and Joseph.

1410
01:25:14,692 --> 01:25:17,779
You have to say something nice,
something like,

1411
01:25:17,862 --> 01:25:21,658
"My mother, she's a loving person.

1412
01:25:21,741 --> 01:25:24,369
-"She's hard working…"
-[all laughing]

1413
01:25:26,246 --> 01:25:29,082
Hey, Rene, you've been laughing
the whole time,

1414
01:25:29,165 --> 01:25:32,418
chuckling away, come on then.

1415
01:25:32,502 --> 01:25:34,003
Let's hear it.

1416
01:25:36,214 --> 01:25:37,549
Come on, Rene.

1417
01:25:37,632 --> 01:25:39,509
[all laughing]

1418
01:25:39,592 --> 01:25:42,303
The fuck! Come on, say it.

1419
01:25:42,387 --> 01:25:43,680
All right, all right…

1420
01:25:45,932 --> 01:25:47,684
[laughing]

1421
01:25:47,767 --> 01:25:51,479
Did you know, the very first time

1422
01:25:51,563 --> 01:25:53,439
I met Paz,

1423
01:25:53,523 --> 01:25:57,485
she was already a celebrity.
Always in the news,

1424
01:25:57,569 --> 01:26:00,280
because she was dating everyone.

1425
01:26:00,363 --> 01:26:05,535
Did you know that she dated a famous
well-known actor.

1426
01:26:07,328 --> 01:26:09,622
-Do you blame me?
-Do you remember?

1427
01:26:10,290 --> 01:26:12,333
He was always…

1428
01:26:12,417 --> 01:26:14,502
-that guy who was--
-Dammit, Rene!

1429
01:26:14,586 --> 01:26:17,589
This is what will remain with you
after I'm dead?

1430
01:26:17,672 --> 01:26:19,883
[all laughing]

1431
01:26:24,095 --> 01:26:25,471
God!

1432
01:26:27,515 --> 01:26:28,766
Insane.

1433
01:26:29,350 --> 01:26:31,102
You're crazy, Rene.

1434
01:26:32,687 --> 01:26:35,607
Hey, Joanne now.

1435
01:26:35,690 --> 01:26:38,818
Brilliant writer. Say something inspiring.

1436
01:26:38,902 --> 01:26:41,446
You know, for your mom.
Come on. Please.

1437
01:26:42,488 --> 01:26:45,074
-Come on. It'll be easy for you.
-No.

1438
01:26:46,159 --> 01:26:48,203
-No.
-Come on, guys.

1439
01:26:48,286 --> 01:26:50,371
You're all so…

1440
01:26:50,455 --> 01:26:52,665
Hey, okay, okay, let's do it this way.

1441
01:26:53,416 --> 01:26:54,500
Jo, take notes.

1442
01:26:56,252 --> 01:27:02,050
"She embraced her world fully
and lived her life fearlessly,

1443
01:27:02,133 --> 01:27:04,969
"but sadly life wasn't so kind to her.

1444
01:27:05,887 --> 01:27:09,224
"She was battered by painful experiences,

1445
01:27:10,308 --> 01:27:11,476
"nevertheless…

1446
01:27:12,393 --> 01:27:15,647
"she remained selfless and generous."

1447
01:27:17,523 --> 01:27:18,775
There you go.

1448
01:27:20,318 --> 01:27:24,405
All right, it could be different.
It could be like this. Take two.

1449
01:27:24,906 --> 01:27:28,534
"She embraced the world fully.

1450
01:27:29,327 --> 01:27:32,038
"She lived her life fiercely,

1451
01:27:33,039 --> 01:27:36,918
"unfortunately life wasn't so kind to her.

1452
01:27:38,253 --> 01:27:41,089
"And she was battered
by painful experiences.

1453
01:27:41,839 --> 01:27:44,884
"Nevertheless, she remained selfless

1454
01:27:45,843 --> 01:27:47,428
"and generous."

1455
01:27:48,012 --> 01:27:49,180
Not bad, huh?

1456
01:27:49,264 --> 01:27:51,349
Okay, Paz, our Paz…

1457
01:27:52,684 --> 01:27:54,185
our shining star.

1458
01:27:54,269 --> 01:27:55,937
Oh, that's so good.

1459
01:27:56,020 --> 01:27:57,855
"Our shining star

1460
01:27:58,356 --> 01:28:01,901
"has taken her rightful place
among the stars.

1461
01:28:03,027 --> 01:28:05,488
"She was not only a great actress,

1462
01:28:05,571 --> 01:28:08,616
"she was also a loving daughter,

1463
01:28:10,201 --> 01:28:13,413
"a kind sister, a loyal partner…

1464
01:28:15,248 --> 01:28:17,667
-"and most of all, she was…
-[Jo thuds]

1465
01:28:19,002 --> 01:28:22,422
Joanne, I know, you wanna say something.

1466
01:28:22,505 --> 01:28:24,132
-Joanne?
-No.

1467
01:28:24,757 --> 01:28:25,717
Okay.

1468
01:28:28,177 --> 01:28:30,221
"Maria Paz Del La Santos…

1469
01:28:32,849 --> 01:28:35,768
"a wonderful, wonderful mother."

1470
01:28:38,479 --> 01:28:39,731
That's it.

1471
01:28:42,275 --> 01:28:44,694
-Hmm?
-Bullshit.

1472
01:28:45,278 --> 01:28:46,946
-Did you say something?
-[slams cutlery]

1473
01:28:48,865 --> 01:28:50,908
If you have something to say, say it.
Come on.

1474
01:28:51,659 --> 01:28:54,579
-What?
-How would I know what to say,

1475
01:28:54,662 --> 01:28:57,332
-when you're a stranger?
-So, you're blaming me?

1476
01:28:58,041 --> 01:28:59,334
Who else, Ma?

1477
01:28:59,959 --> 01:29:01,336
Or maybe it's my fault then?

1478
01:29:01,419 --> 01:29:03,338
Okay, before you say anything,
I'd shut up.

1479
01:29:04,630 --> 01:29:07,008
You don't understand anything.

1480
01:29:07,091 --> 01:29:08,968
Please make me understand.

1481
01:29:10,011 --> 01:29:11,929
You have no idea what I went through.

1482
01:29:12,555 --> 01:29:13,806
How it wasn't easy…

1483
01:29:15,308 --> 01:29:17,935
After I gave birth to you,
I had to quit working.

1484
01:29:18,686 --> 01:29:21,147
I had to settle down with your father,

1485
01:29:21,230 --> 01:29:23,733
be a good wife, be a good mother.

1486
01:29:24,275 --> 01:29:26,527
I had to take care of your Nono.

1487
01:29:27,820 --> 01:29:29,864
I had to give up my career!

1488
01:29:30,406 --> 01:29:32,867
Nobody wanted to employ you, Ma.

1489
01:29:33,534 --> 01:29:35,036
Why can't you just accept it?

1490
01:29:35,119 --> 01:29:37,163
I was protecting you, Joanne.

1491
01:29:37,246 --> 01:29:38,539
I was protecting you.

1492
01:29:38,623 --> 01:29:40,458
If I hadn't left…

1493
01:29:40,541 --> 01:29:43,086
I could have put myself in danger,
you in danger…

1494
01:29:43,169 --> 01:29:44,462
And what happened?

1495
01:29:44,962 --> 01:29:46,547
I was still hurt by you.

1496
01:29:48,591 --> 01:29:52,386
And now, since you're out of money
and you're sick…

1497
01:29:52,470 --> 01:29:53,805
you're back for Round 2,

1498
01:29:53,888 --> 01:29:55,807
as if nothing ever happened.

1499
01:29:55,890 --> 01:29:58,851
And you expect us to drop everything.

1500
01:29:58,935 --> 01:30:00,937
I never asked you to take care of me!

1501
01:30:03,439 --> 01:30:04,440
Never!

1502
01:30:06,526 --> 01:30:08,361
Why did you want me to be here?

1503
01:30:09,153 --> 01:30:12,907
'Cause I wanted to see if you're okay
before I died.

1504
01:30:12,990 --> 01:30:14,200
Hmm.

1505
01:30:14,283 --> 01:30:17,203
To assuage your guilt,
you travelled back home

1506
01:30:17,954 --> 01:30:21,582
to check if the daughter you left
managed to do okay anyway.

1507
01:30:23,000 --> 01:30:25,169
Our your fucking sin first.

1508
01:30:25,253 --> 01:30:28,256
Oh, my god… Joanne.

1509
01:30:29,882 --> 01:30:32,260
Why do you have
so much hate in your heart?

1510
01:30:32,343 --> 01:30:34,011
Oh! [chuckles]

1511
01:30:34,095 --> 01:30:36,180
So much? Yes, Ma!

1512
01:30:37,890 --> 01:30:40,434
Because of how long you left me for…

1513
01:30:41,477 --> 01:30:45,064
not one explanation.

1514
01:30:47,567 --> 01:30:51,279
You left me when I was a child!

1515
01:30:52,822 --> 01:30:54,448
Why, Ma?

1516
01:30:54,532 --> 01:30:56,159
Why?

1517
01:30:56,242 --> 01:30:58,786
Explain to me now, what I did wrong?

1518
01:30:58,870 --> 01:31:00,580
-I was--
-How did I fail?

1519
01:31:00,663 --> 01:31:02,456
I was not well.

1520
01:31:05,376 --> 01:31:06,711
Not well?

1521
01:31:10,256 --> 01:31:11,507
Okay.

1522
01:31:14,552 --> 01:31:17,221
That's why you left for "America"?

1523
01:31:18,431 --> 01:31:20,725
To be single again? To…

1524
01:31:21,225 --> 01:31:24,520
find another man
and give birth to another child?

1525
01:31:24,604 --> 01:31:26,731
You have no right to judge me.

1526
01:31:28,524 --> 01:31:31,903
You have no fucking clue
what I went through in New York!

1527
01:31:33,821 --> 01:31:35,406
Well, you think you're…

1528
01:31:35,489 --> 01:31:37,033
so fucking smart!

1529
01:31:37,116 --> 01:31:39,118
I had to become smart.

1530
01:31:41,871 --> 01:31:45,833
I had to parent myself for 27 years!

1531
01:31:46,542 --> 01:31:47,960
You weren't there!

1532
01:31:51,547 --> 01:31:53,841
And yet, I made something of myself.

1533
01:31:56,427 --> 01:31:57,637
And you…

1534
01:32:00,139 --> 01:32:01,599
look at you.

1535
01:32:01,682 --> 01:32:03,601
Your life went nowhere.

1536
01:32:04,393 --> 01:32:06,854
You know, when you were gone…

1537
01:32:08,731 --> 01:32:10,316
I was okay.

1538
01:32:10,399 --> 01:32:11,901
[thunder rumbling]

1539
01:32:16,072 --> 01:32:17,531
Well then, good for you.

1540
01:32:19,784 --> 01:32:24,580
I'm so happy that you found peace
through therapy…

1541
01:32:25,581 --> 01:32:26,749
with…

1542
01:32:27,416 --> 01:32:30,127
that handsome psychiatrist you're fucking.

1543
01:32:31,629 --> 01:32:32,755
Well shit…

1544
01:32:34,882 --> 01:32:36,217
who's selfish now?

1545
01:32:37,551 --> 01:32:39,971
I'm putting my dreams on hold

1546
01:32:40,054 --> 01:32:42,139
because I wanna be here for you.

1547
01:32:42,223 --> 01:32:44,183
I never asked you to.

1548
01:32:44,267 --> 01:32:45,810
I'm not like you!

1549
01:32:45,893 --> 01:32:48,187
I can't just
ignore my conscience like you.

1550
01:32:49,313 --> 01:32:51,274
Abandoning a loved one.

1551
01:32:51,357 --> 01:32:52,650
Now, there it is.

1552
01:32:54,360 --> 01:32:55,820
You finally said it.

1553
01:32:58,447 --> 01:33:01,492
So the whole reason you're here,

1554
01:33:02,076 --> 01:33:04,036
is not for anything, but for you

1555
01:33:04,954 --> 01:33:07,331
to feel better about yourself.

1556
01:33:07,415 --> 01:33:11,919
Or, is it to show everyone
that you're so much better than

1557
01:33:12,003 --> 01:33:14,505
your loser mother. Is that it?

1558
01:33:14,588 --> 01:33:17,008
Is that your dramatic through line?

1559
01:33:20,928 --> 01:33:22,471
You're not any better.

1560
01:33:23,848 --> 01:33:27,768
You come from a long line
of narcissistic, proud people

1561
01:33:27,852 --> 01:33:30,104
who would gladly sweep

1562
01:33:30,855 --> 01:33:33,566
difficult conversations under the rug,

1563
01:33:33,649 --> 01:33:37,611
and pretend that everything is fine
until it's not.

1564
01:33:39,780 --> 01:33:41,073
And then we escape.

1565
01:33:41,157 --> 01:33:42,825
Because that's what we do,

1566
01:33:42,908 --> 01:33:44,243
you and I, both.

1567
01:33:44,910 --> 01:33:47,580
-Mom, please. If you'd only--
-What?

1568
01:33:47,663 --> 01:33:49,332
Huh? Be sorry?

1569
01:33:51,292 --> 01:33:52,752
[thunder rumbling]

1570
01:33:52,835 --> 01:33:54,628
[loud thunderclap]

1571
01:33:59,508 --> 01:34:01,260
[wind blowing]

1572
01:34:11,896 --> 01:34:13,439
Look after yourself, okay.

1573
01:34:19,403 --> 01:34:21,572
-[Bes] Jo, darling!.
-Mom.

1574
01:34:21,655 --> 01:34:23,741
You phone. [exhales]

1575
01:34:27,495 --> 01:34:28,996
Say goodbye to your mother.

1576
01:34:41,300 --> 01:34:42,927
[breath shaking]

1577
01:34:45,721 --> 01:34:47,056
I love you.

1578
01:34:47,932 --> 01:34:49,683
-Take care.
-Love you.

1579
01:35:28,889 --> 01:35:31,016
<i>-Uh, hi.</i>
-Hi, Ben.

1580
01:35:31,100 --> 01:35:33,894
<i>-Jo?</i>
-Sorry, did I wake you?

1581
01:35:33,978 --> 01:35:35,354
<i>No, no. That's fine.</i>

1582
01:35:35,438 --> 01:35:37,565
I just emailed the final treatment.

1583
01:35:37,648 --> 01:35:39,775
<i>You did! And that's great to hear.</i>

1584
01:35:39,859 --> 01:35:42,027
-Yeah, let's do this.
<i>-Great, Jo.</i>

1585
01:35:42,111 --> 01:35:45,030
<i>Uh… you don't sound too happy though.</i>

1586
01:35:45,114 --> 01:35:46,198
<i>You okay?</i>

1587
01:35:46,282 --> 01:35:48,451
-I'm just tired.
<i>-Okay, then.</i>

1588
01:35:50,286 --> 01:35:54,123
<i>Can you make here next week,</i>
<i>like Tuesday?</i>

1589
01:35:54,206 --> 01:35:56,250
<i>-What do you think?</i>
-Tuesday?

1590
01:35:56,333 --> 01:35:58,210
<i>Yeah, there is a chance--</i>

1591
01:35:59,753 --> 01:36:00,671
Hello?

1592
01:36:22,026 --> 01:36:23,277
[knock at door]

1593
01:36:25,362 --> 01:36:26,739
[knock at door]

1594
01:36:29,450 --> 01:36:31,577
-[banging]
-Just wait.

1595
01:36:35,372 --> 01:36:36,957
-Hi.
-Hey.

1596
01:36:37,041 --> 01:36:39,335
-What? You're here!
-Yeah.

1597
01:36:40,294 --> 01:36:41,295
You left this.

1598
01:36:43,631 --> 01:36:46,008
-Oh, thank you!
-No problem.

1599
01:36:49,011 --> 01:36:50,513
Oh, it's just me.

1600
01:36:50,596 --> 01:36:53,182
I took the bus here,
And aunt Des taught me.

1601
01:36:53,265 --> 01:36:55,309
-See?
-Oh… okay.

1602
01:36:57,686 --> 01:36:59,563
-Well, I gotta go. See ya.
-Hey.

1603
01:36:59,647 --> 01:37:02,566
-Matti, stop. Come in.
-Really?

1604
01:37:02,650 --> 01:37:04,318
-Yeah!
-All right.

1605
01:37:04,401 --> 01:37:06,612
I'll take you to the station tomorrow.

1606
01:37:15,371 --> 01:37:16,497
So…

1607
01:37:18,499 --> 01:37:21,001
are you hungry? Have you eaten?
Come on.

1608
01:37:23,170 --> 01:37:24,797
I have, well…

1609
01:37:24,880 --> 01:37:27,007
leftover pasta and beer.

1610
01:37:27,091 --> 01:37:28,634
Ow, what kind of beer?

1611
01:37:30,344 --> 01:37:32,846
-It's just beer.
-Whatever.

1612
01:37:33,347 --> 01:37:34,765
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

1613
01:37:42,856 --> 01:37:44,441
I'm leaving next week.

1614
01:37:46,443 --> 01:37:47,570
Already?

1615
01:37:48,237 --> 01:37:50,906
I was about to leave
when you guys arrived.

1616
01:37:53,784 --> 01:37:54,868
You excited?

1617
01:37:56,745 --> 01:37:57,788
Nervous.

1618
01:37:58,581 --> 01:37:59,623
You'll survive.

1619
01:38:00,791 --> 01:38:02,585
You are mom's daughter after all.

1620
01:38:03,085 --> 01:38:04,169
Hmm.

1621
01:38:07,381 --> 01:38:08,674
How's your mom?

1622
01:38:09,925 --> 01:38:11,010
You know…

1623
01:38:12,386 --> 01:38:13,220
still a…

1624
01:38:13,846 --> 01:38:16,140
-bitch.
-[both chuckle]

1625
01:38:19,268 --> 01:38:20,269
[exhales softly]

1626
01:38:23,981 --> 01:38:25,649
You never ran away?

1627
01:38:25,733 --> 01:38:27,401
-From mom?
-Hmm.

1628
01:38:28,611 --> 01:38:29,612
Never.

1629
01:38:32,156 --> 01:38:35,117
You know, even while she'd be screaming
at me,

1630
01:38:36,493 --> 01:38:38,412
I still felt that she loved me.

1631
01:38:40,831 --> 01:38:43,417
I love how we'd watch movies together,

1632
01:38:44,001 --> 01:38:45,836
and I'd curl up on the couch next to her…

1633
01:38:48,422 --> 01:38:51,300
and I even love the way she smells
like cigarettes all the time.

1634
01:38:53,093 --> 01:38:54,094
It's kind of weird.

1635
01:38:55,554 --> 01:38:59,767
You know, in New York,
we would take walks on Sundays,

1636
01:39:00,809 --> 01:39:04,438
and she would tell me about
the Philippines and how beautiful it was,

1637
01:39:04,521 --> 01:39:05,856
and yadda, yadda, yadda.

1638
01:39:06,565 --> 01:39:10,402
{\an8}And she would tell me about
how much of herself she saw in you.

1639
01:39:12,571 --> 01:39:14,990
{\an8}And then, she would just be quiet
for a few blocks…

1640
01:39:17,368 --> 01:39:19,662
{\an8}and we would just walk and walk,

1641
01:39:20,412 --> 01:39:21,997
{\an8}and she wouldn't say anything.

1642
01:39:24,083 --> 01:39:25,334
{\an8}And I always wondered why.

1643
01:39:27,169 --> 01:39:28,796
{\an8}Maybe she was thinking of you.

1644
01:39:32,758 --> 01:39:34,218
In fact, I know she was.

1645
01:39:44,561 --> 01:39:46,313
[traffic noise]

1646
01:39:50,693 --> 01:39:52,111
Hey, you don't have to wait for me.

1647
01:39:52,194 --> 01:39:53,612
-I won't get lost.
-Bus is leaving.

1648
01:39:53,696 --> 01:39:56,323
It's okay. Lemme check
if this is the right one.

1649
01:39:56,407 --> 01:39:57,825
[man] Come on. Get in.

1650
01:39:59,952 --> 01:40:02,788
-Does bus to go Lucena?
-It does, ma'am.

1651
01:40:02,871 --> 01:40:04,957
-Hurry up, we're about to leave.
-This is the one.

1652
01:40:05,040 --> 01:40:06,333
Well, I guess this is it.

1653
01:40:07,501 --> 01:40:11,338
Good luck in New York, and grab a slice
of pizza for me while you're there.

1654
01:40:11,839 --> 01:40:14,049
Okay. Sure.

1655
01:40:17,219 --> 01:40:18,512
Uh…

1656
01:40:20,889 --> 01:40:24,601
-You didn't take a shower. Gross.
-I need the instructions to get back home.

1657
01:40:24,685 --> 01:40:26,937
-All those to Lucena, we're leaving now.
-See ya.

1658
01:40:28,439 --> 01:40:29,773
Take care.

1659
01:40:29,857 --> 01:40:31,024
Come on. Get a seat.

1660
01:40:39,199 --> 01:40:40,993
[bus reversing]

1661
01:40:44,413 --> 01:40:45,789
[chuckles]

1662
01:40:57,551 --> 01:40:59,720
[soft piano music playing]

1663
01:41:16,528 --> 01:41:17,613
[bus honks]

1664
01:41:21,575 --> 01:41:24,328
Bus driver! Wait!

1665
01:41:25,412 --> 01:41:27,080
[music continues]

1666
01:43:21,278 --> 01:43:23,322
[heart beating]

1667
01:43:49,681 --> 01:43:52,184
[Matti playing Spanish guitar]

1668
01:44:54,955 --> 01:44:56,748
[birds chirping]

1669
01:45:32,743 --> 01:45:33,744
-Pa?
-Hmm.

1670
01:45:34,327 --> 01:45:35,829
There's no disguising this crack.

1671
01:45:37,497 --> 01:45:38,582
It's all right.

1672
01:45:39,166 --> 01:45:40,917
Perfection can be overrated.

1673
01:45:51,428 --> 01:45:52,679
Darling.

1674
01:45:54,848 --> 01:45:56,349
Please find it withing you

1675
01:45:57,392 --> 01:45:59,561
to forgive me for not opening up to you.

1676
01:46:01,354 --> 01:46:03,565
You should know that my family

1677
01:46:04,107 --> 01:46:05,400
didn't talk a lot.

1678
01:46:06,568 --> 01:46:08,278
To speak up was taboo.

1679
01:46:10,906 --> 01:46:12,783
But thing that's important…

1680
01:46:14,534 --> 01:46:17,120
is that I love you
more than I can possibly tell you.

1681
01:46:25,796 --> 01:46:27,798
It looks like you got a scratch there.

1682
01:46:28,423 --> 01:46:30,092
Oh, that's… [chuckles]

1683
01:46:31,093 --> 01:46:33,178
I got this scar when I was a child.

1684
01:46:35,514 --> 01:46:36,890
Forgot it was there.

1685
01:46:41,311 --> 01:46:43,021
Some wounds last forever.

1686
01:46:52,114 --> 01:46:55,117
Matti! Matti, come here!

1687
01:46:55,951 --> 01:46:57,077
Your mom's ready!

1688
01:46:58,620 --> 01:47:00,413
-Get over here!
-Coming.

1689
01:47:02,999 --> 01:47:05,210
[Jo] They really put here in here?

1690
01:47:05,293 --> 01:47:06,920
[Des] This choice was your mother's.

1691
01:47:08,004 --> 01:47:09,464
Okay.

1692
01:47:09,548 --> 01:47:11,049
-Still grumpy.
-[all chuckle]

1693
01:47:12,175 --> 01:47:15,095
When we get to the sea,
we'll scatter Paz's ashes,

1694
01:47:15,178 --> 01:47:18,014
and we all have to smiling as we do it!

1695
01:47:18,098 --> 01:47:20,267
Your mom wouldn't want to see us sad.

1696
01:47:24,437 --> 01:47:25,522
Okay.

1697
01:47:27,107 --> 01:47:28,817
Here we go!

1698
01:47:28,900 --> 01:47:31,236
Are we supposed to say a prayer
or something?

1699
01:47:31,945 --> 01:47:34,156
Uh… my lord,

1700
01:47:34,865 --> 01:47:36,575
thank you for the wind,

1701
01:47:36,658 --> 01:47:38,160
the rain,

1702
01:47:38,243 --> 01:47:40,495
and even for the storms we endure.

1703
01:47:41,246 --> 01:47:43,832
And for sun at daybreak, thank you.

1704
01:47:45,041 --> 01:47:46,084
Amen.

1705
01:47:46,960 --> 01:47:48,461
[all] Amen!

1706
01:47:49,379 --> 01:47:54,426
[Des] One, two… smile and three, go!

1707
01:47:54,509 --> 01:47:56,469
[coughing and laughing]

1708
01:48:00,432 --> 01:48:01,474
Take another one.

1709
01:48:02,475 --> 01:48:05,228
-Going again.
-One, two, three…

1710
01:48:05,312 --> 01:48:07,814
[coughing and laughing]

1711
01:48:13,236 --> 01:48:14,779
[all yelping joyfully]

1712
01:48:17,657 --> 01:48:19,492
[playful laughter]

1713
01:48:30,587 --> 01:48:31,880
Mama!

1714
01:48:33,340 --> 01:48:34,549
[all whooping]

1715
01:48:37,886 --> 01:48:40,847
[somber song playing]